<.shell title="Confirm dialog" current={:confirm_dialog}>
  <h1>Confirm dialog</h1>
  <p class="lead">A question before a change that can't be undone.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.button id="confirm-dialog-demo" variant={:danger}>Delete clause</.button>
    <.confirm_dialog
      message="Delete the First Aid clause? Its 3 qualifications are removed from the group rule."
      action="Delete clause"
      variant="btn-danger"
    />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>Before a delete or a send that can't be undone.</p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>A change that can be undone, or one the person reviews on the page first.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The question names the thing and says what happens.</li>
    <li>
      The action button repeats the label and colour of the button that asked. The other is Cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      It is our own dialog, not the browser's: some phone browsers never show <code>window.confirm</code>, so the button did nothing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    document.getElementById("confirm-dialog-demo").addEventListener("click", function () {
      document.getElementById("confirm-dialog").showModal();
    });
  </script>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>data-confirm="…"</code>
    on the button. The root layout renders <code>&lt;.confirm_dialog /&gt;</code>
    once, and <code>assets/js/confirm_dialog.js</code>
    opens it.
  </p>
</.shell>
